.pytest_tmp/

# Generated design preview: a static jsdom capture of index.html with mock
# findings and styles.css inlined. Regenerate it rather than editing it.
web/design-preview.html

# Generated tooling output, not a source artefact.
docs/security-audit/

# Local working documents live in .git/info/exclude, NOT here. This file is
# published; naming a withheld document in it discloses that the document
# exists and what it is called, which is the disclosure the exclusion was
# meant to prevent. .git/info/exclude is never committed, so it ignores them
# locally without shipping their names.

# Stale git lock files renamed aside. Harmless and empty.
aside-*.lock

g.sh

# Draft rules awaiting approval -- generated by ingestion, not source. A first
# import produces one draft file per Data Dictionary; they are inert until
# approved, and approving one writes to Rules/<pack>/.../rules/ instead.
.drafts/

docs/audits/

# Per-pack ingestion by-products, rebuilt from the source documents: the hash
# of each document last ingested, and the obligations parsed out of it. A tree
# without those documents must not carry a cache that describes them, or the
# application starts by reporting entries it cannot see. Already-tracked copies
# are unaffected; this keeps regenerated ones out of a fresh clone.
.ingestion_state.json
.dd_obligations.json
